1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:02,974
There are over 8 billion people on Earth.

2
00:00:02,974 --> 00:00:05,065
But what if we're all related?

3
00:00:05,065 --> 00:00:06,928
Let's climb our friend's family tree.

4
00:00:06,928 --> 00:00:09,504
He has 2 parents, 4 grandparents,

5
00:00:09,504 --> 00:00:11,124
and 8 great-grandparents.

6
00:00:11,124 --> 00:00:13,710
Every generation back, the number doubles!

7
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:16,568
30 generations back, about 800 years ago,

8
00:00:16,568 --> 00:00:17,514
his tree has over

9
00:00:17,514 --> 00:00:19,622
a billion ancestor slots. But back then,

10
00:00:19,622 --> 00:00:21,249
the whole world had only about

11
00:00:21,249 --> 00:00:23,746
400 million people. So the same people

12
00:00:23,746 --> 00:00:25,893
fill many slots, again and again.

13
00:00:25,893 --> 00:00:27,229
And everyone's family trees

14
00:00:27,229 --> 00:00:29,262
start to overlap. One model suggests

15
00:00:29,262 --> 00:00:31,603
everyone alive today may share an ancestor

16
00:00:31,603 --> 00:00:33,864
from just a few thousand years ago.

17
00:00:33,864 --> 00:00:36,013
Now let's rewind much further.

18
00:00:36,013 --> 00:00:37,342
Your family tree covers

19
00:00:37,342 --> 00:00:38,751
everyone you descend from.

20
00:00:38,751 --> 00:00:39,788
Your DNA carries pieces

21
00:00:39,788 --> 00:00:42,017
from only some of them. DNA passed from

22
00:00:42,017 --> 00:00:43,522
mother to child traces back to

23
00:00:43,522 --> 00:00:46,821
one woman in Africa, about 150,000–200,000

24
00:00:46,821 --> 00:00:48,603
years ago. Scientists call her

25
00:00:48,603 --> 00:00:51,038
Mitochondrial Eve. DNA passed from

26
00:00:51,038 --> 00:00:53,164
father to son traces men back to one man:

27
00:00:53,164 --> 00:00:55,825
Y-chromosomal Adam. They weren't a couple,

28
00:00:55,825 --> 00:00:56,790
and probably didn't even

29
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:57,920
live at the same time.

30
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:58,559
Scientists can trace

31
00:00:58,559 --> 00:00:59,836
certain genetic lineages

32
00:00:59,836 --> 00:01:00,953
back to common ancestors.

33
00:01:00,953 --> 00:01:02,580
But these weren't the only people

34
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:04,561
alive at the time. Their lines are simply

35
00:01:04,561 --> 00:01:06,201
the ones that never broke.

36
00:01:06,201 --> 00:01:08,009
Later, people moved out of Africa

37
00:01:08,009 --> 00:01:09,235
and spread across the globe,

38
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:10,756
into Asia, Europe, Australia,

39
00:01:10,756 --> 00:01:13,399
and the Americas. Just think about it.

40
00:01:13,399 --> 00:01:15,671
Everyone watching this, in Japan, Brazil,

41
00:01:15,671 --> 00:01:18,516
or Turkey, is your distant relative.

42
00:01:18,516 --> 00:01:20,317
8 billion people. Billions of

43
00:01:20,317 --> 00:01:22,115
family stories. And a past that's

44
00:01:22,115 --> 00:01:24,225
far more connected than you think.

